# Compilation of observed intracluster-light / intracluster-star mass fractions
#
#   f_ICS = m_ICS / M_*,halo    with  M_*,halo = m_ICS + m_BCG + sum(m_satellites)
#
# for groups and clusters between z = 0 and z = 2.  Assembled from the
# observational compilation used in the SAGE26 ICS figures
# (SAGE26/plotting/random_plotting_scripts/BCG_ICS_fraction.py), which digitised
# each of the sources listed below.  Simulation curves in that figure
# (Rudick et al. 2011, Tang et al. 2018) are deliberately NOT included here.
#
# Caveats, all inherent to the literature rather than to this file:
#   * Individual measurements carry no published uncertainty in the source
#     compilation, so the constraint (src/constraints.py, class FICS) derives the
#     error bar from the scatter between independent measurements in each
#     redshift bin.  That scatter is dominated by the systematic disagreement
#     between ICL definitions, which is the honest error budget here.
#   * The ICL/BCG split is definition dependent: surface-brightness cuts,
#     double-Sersic decompositions and aperture choices give systematically
#     different fractions for the same cluster.  Points from different sources at
#     the same redshift therefore need not agree.
#   * Montes & Trujillo (2018) contributes two marker sets (a, b) in the source
#     figure, corresponding to their two measurement methods; both are retained,
#     so a few clusters appear twice at the same redshift.
#   * The Montes & Trujillo (2018a) entry with f_ICS = 0 is a digitisation
#     artefact and is filtered out by the loader; it is kept here for provenance.
#   * Group samples (Ragusa+23 VEGAS groups, Ahad+25 KiDS+GAMA groups) probe
#     M_vir ~ 10^12.5-10^13.5; the cluster samples probe 10^14-10^15.  Those two
#     sets are 25 and 61 of the 86 usable points respectively, and the group
#     points sit systematically LOWER: excluding them would raise the z < 0.3 bin
#     medians from 0.18/0.15/0.16 to 0.23/0.20/0.21.  All of them are used.  The
#     FICS constraint therefore keeps its model halo-mass floor low
#     (FICS_MVIR_MIN = 10^12) so the model averages over group and cluster
#     scales together, as this compilation does.
#
# Sources:
#   Burke12            Burke, Collins, Stott & Hilton (2012), ICL at z ~ 1
#   MontesTrujillo18a  Montes & Trujillo (2018), ICL at the Frontier (method a)
#   Burke15            Burke, Hilton & Collins (2015), ICL and CLASH
#   Furnell21          Furnell et al. (2021), ICL growth in XCS-HSC, 0.1<z<0.5
#   Feldmeier04        Feldmeier et al. (2004), deep CCD imaging
#   MontesTrujillo18b  Montes & Trujillo (2018), ICL at the Frontier (method b)
#   KoJee18            Ko & Jee (2018), ICL at z = 1.24
#   Kluge21            Kluge et al. (2021), ICL and its host cluster
#   Zibetti05          Zibetti et al. (2005), intergalactic stars at z = 0.25
#   Presotto14a/b      Presotto et al. (2014), MACS J1206.2-0847 (two estimates)
#   Spavone20          Spavone et al. (2020), Fornax Deep Survey
#   XLSSC122           JWST imaging of XLSSC 122 at z = 1.98
#   Ragusa23_groups    Ragusa et al. (2023), VEGAS groups
#   Ragusa23_Antlia    Ragusa et al. (2023), VEGAS Antlia cluster
#   Ahad25             Ahad et al. (2025), KiDS+GAMA groups
#
# Columns:
#   1  z        redshift
#   2  f_ICS    m_ICS / M_*,halo
#   3  source   short reference tag
#
#         z      f_ICS  source
